# Federated neighbourhood of eight interfaces of an ornithopter demonstrator, in the shape the interface CONSTRUCT produces.
#   IF-01  FR J11 / DE P11 plugs coincide; the FR control post is releasable to FR only  -> pass, hidden from non-FR viewers
#   IF-02  DE J21 / FR P21: 4.3 mm apart on x                                            -> position
#   IF-03  FR J31 / DE P31: 55 vs 37 pins                                                -> connector
#   IF-04  DE RF-4 / ES CC-4 fasteners: 6.35 mm vs 7.94 mm; HY-4 / HZ-4 couplings match  -> fastener
#   IF-05  FR J51 (mm) / UK HC 51 (inches) plugs, RF-5 / FS 5 fasteners (mm vs inches),
#          HY-5 / HYD 5 couplings (bar vs psi): all coincide after conversion             -> pass
#   IF-06  UK HC 61 positions carry no unit; HY-6 350 bar vs HYD 6 3000 psi                -> unit, hydraulic
#   IF-07  DE P71 has no mate; the DE tail trim drive is EXPORT-LICENCE, releasable to
#          licensed recipients only                                                       -> orphan, hidden from EU viewers
#   IF-08  ES J82 / ES P82 plugs coincide; the ES tail plane has no tag                   -> pass, hidden from all but the export officer
# Parts carry their PLM description (label, sourceFileRef), their file-index CAD file and, except
# the untagged tail plane, their Atelier core tag (jurisdiction, releasableTo, taggedBy, taggedAt).
# The control post alone is supplier-built: the file index carries its atelier:builtBy.
# Three Atelier core products. The ornithopter holds every part; the wings hold the mid cross beam, the
# left wing root fitting and the left wing actuator (the wings state no frame); the tail holds the tail
# boom, the tail trim drive and the tail plane (a hidden and an untagged part). Each interface belongs
# to one product (atelier:ofProduct, and the product segment of its IRI): IF-01 to IF-04 to the
# ornithopter, IF-05 and IF-06 to the wings, IF-07 and IF-08 to the tail. Scoping to the ornithopter
# therefore lists its own four interfaces and the parts they name.
@prefix atelier:  <https://example.com/atelier/ontology#> .
@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ifo:  <https://example.com/atelier/interface/ornithopter/> .
@prefix ifw:  <https://example.com/atelier/interface/wings/> .
@prefix ift:  <https://example.com/atelier/interface/tail/> .
@prefix frp:  <https://example.com/atelier/fr/plug/> .
@prefix dep:  <https://example.com/atelier/de/plug/> .
@prefix ukp:  <https://example.com/atelier/uk/plug/> .
@prefix esp:  <https://example.com/atelier/es/plug/> .
@prefix frf:  <https://example.com/atelier/fr/fastener/> .
@prefix def:  <https://example.com/atelier/de/fastener/> .
@prefix esf:  <https://example.com/atelier/es/fastener/> .
@prefix frc:  <https://example.com/atelier/fr/coupling/> .
@prefix dec:  <https://example.com/atelier/de/coupling/> .
@prefix esc:  <https://example.com/atelier/es/coupling/> .
@prefix frpt: <https://example.com/atelier/fr/part/> .
@prefix dept: <https://example.com/atelier/de/part/> .
@prefix ukpt: <https://example.com/atelier/uk/part/> .
@prefix espt: <https://example.com/atelier/es/part/> .

